"comparison": "Both Morgan Stanley and Goldman Sachs are defendants in consolidated antitrust actions regarding interest rate swap trading in the SDNY. A key similarity is that both entities saw the court grant preliminary approval of a class action settlement on July 11, 2024. However, a significant difference exists in the scope of litigation and resolution: Goldman Sachs explicitly states that while the class action settlement was approved, the firm has 'paid its full contribution into escrow,' indicating financial resolution for that specific claim. In contrast, Morgan Stanley's disclosure for 2024 only notes the agreement in principle and preliminary approval, without confirming final payment or escrow deposit. Additionally, Goldman Sachs discloses that individual actions (filed by operators of swap execution facilities) remain pending, whereas Morgan Stanley's text focuses primarily on the class claims settlement.",
